} = 0$", "Let me define $f(\\lambda) = 4\\lambda + \\mu - \\sum_i \\frac{M_i}{1 - 2\\lambda M_i}$", "At $\\lambda = 0$: $f(0) = 0 + \\mu - \\sum_i M_i = \\mu - \\mu = 0$. ✓", "Let me try to factor this. Let me write:\n$$\\sum_i \\frac{M_i}{1 - 2\\lambda M_i} = \\sum_i M_i \\cdot \\frac{1}{1 - 2\\lambda M_i}$$", "So: $4\\lambda + \\mu - \\sum_i \\frac{M_i}{1 - 2\\lambda M_i} = 0$", "Let me multiply through by $\\prod_j (1 - 2\\lambda M_j)$:", "$$(4\\lambda + \\mu)\\prod_j(1 - 2\\lambda M_j) - \\sum_i M_i \\prod_{j \\neq i}(1 - 2\\lambda M_j) = 0$$", "This is getting complicated in general. Let me think about specific cases.", "Case 1: All $M_i$ are equal, say $M_i = m$ for all $i = 1, \\ldots, n$.", "Then $\\mu = nm$.\n\nThe equation becomes:\n$$4\\lambda + nm - \\sum_i \\frac{m}{1 - 2\\lambda m} = 0$$\n$$4\\lambda + nm - \\frac{nm}{1 - 2\\lambda m} = 0$$", "Multiply by $(1 - 2\\lambda m)$:\n$$(4\\lambda + nm)(1 - 2\\lambda m) - nm = 0$$\n$$4\\lambda - 8\\lambda^2 m + nm - 2\\lambda m \\cdot nm - nm = 0$$\n$$4\\lambda - 8m\\lambda^2 - 2nm^2\\lambda = 0$$\n$$\\lambda(4 - 8m\\lambda - 2nm^2) = 0$$", "So $\\lambda = 0$ or $\\lambda = \\frac{4}{8m + 2nm^2} = \\frac{4}{2m(4 + nm)} = \\frac{2}{m(4 + nm)}$", "Hmm, so in this special case we get $\\lambda = 0$ and $\\lambda = \\frac{2}{m(nm + 4)}$.", "Let me check: with $M_i = m$, $\\mu = nm$.\n$\\frac{2}{m(nm+4)}$: Let's verify.", "$4\\lambda + nm - \\frac{nm}{1-2\\lambda m} = 0$", "With $\\lambda = \\frac{2}{m(nm+4)}$:\n$2\\lambda m = \\frac{4}{nm+4}$", "$1 - 2\\lambda m = 1 - \\frac{4}{nm+4} = \\frac{nm}{nm+4}$", "$\\frac{nm}{1-2\\lambda m} = \\frac{nm \\cdot (nm+4)}{nm} = nm + 4$", "$4\\lambda = \\frac{8}{m(nm+4)}$", "So: $\\frac{8}{m(nm+4)} + nm - (nm+4) = \\frac{8}{m(nm+4)} - 4$", "$= \\frac{8 - 4m(nm+4)}{m(nm+4)} = \\frac{8 - 4nm^2 - 16m}{m(nm+4)}$", "This is zero only when $8 - 4nm^2 - 16m = 0$, i.e., $nm^2 + 4m - 2 = 0$. So my general solution doesn't work for arbitrary $m$ and $n$.", "Wait, let me redo. $4\\lambda 